Prompt — What You Are Building

Role-based data visibility in SAP BTP using CAP and Fiori.

Two business roles:

User1Role → Can see only persons whose age > 40

User2Role → Can see only persons whose age < 40


When the user logs into the Fiori application:

Their name (from JWT token) must be displayed

The Persons table must automatically filter based on role

Filtering must happen securely in backend (CAP), not in UI


Authentication handled by SAP XSUAA
Backend built with SAP CAP
Frontend built using SAP Fiori


---

END-TO-END IMPLEMENTATION


---

1️⃣ Create CAP Project

cds init age-role-app
cd age-role-app
npm install


---

2️⃣ xs-security.json

Create in project root:

{
  "xsappname": "age-role-app",
  "tenant-mode": "dedicated",
  "scopes": [
    { "name": "$XSAPPNAME.User1", "description": "Age greater than 40" },
    { "name": "$XSAPPNAME.User2", "description": "Age less than 40" }
  ],
  "role-templates": [
    {
      "name": "User1Role",
      "scope-references": ["$XSAPPNAME.User1"]
    },
    {
      "name": "User2Role",
      "scope-references": ["$XSAPPNAME.User2"]
    }
  ]
}


---

3️⃣ Data Model

db/schema.cds

namespace demo;

entity Persons {
  key ID     : UUID;
  name       : String;
  age        : Integer;
  gender     : String;
}


---

4️⃣ Service Definition

srv/service.cds

using demo from '../db/schema';

service PersonService {

  entity Persons as projection on demo.Persons;

  function getLoggedInUser() returns {
    id   : String;
    name : String;
  };

}


---

5️⃣ Service Logic (Role-Based Filtering)

srv/service.js

const cds = require('@sap/cds');

module.exports = (srv) => {

  const { Persons } = srv.entities;

  // ROLE-BASED FILTERING
  srv.before('READ', Persons, (req) => {

    if (req.user.is('User1Role')) {
      req.query.where({ age: { '>': 40 } });
    }

    if (req.user.is('User2Role')) {
      req.query.where({ age: { '<': 40 } });
    }

  });

  // RETURN LOGGED-IN USER
  srv.on('getLoggedInUser', (req) => {

    return {
      id: req.user.id,
      name: req.user.attr.givenName + " " + req.user.attr.familyName
    };

  });

};


---

6️⃣ Enable XSUAA in package.json

"cds": {
  "requires": {
    "auth": "xsuaa"
  }
}


---

7️⃣ Deploy to BTP

Create XSUAA service:

cf create-service xsuaa application age-role-xsuaa -c xs-security.json

Create role collections in BTP cockpit:

Assign User1Role to User A

Assign User2Role to User B


Deploy:

mbt build
cf deploy mta_archives/age-role-app_1.0.0.mtar


---

8️⃣ Create Fiori App

In SAP Business Application Studio: Create Freestyle UI5 App.

Add destination pointing to CAP service.


---

9️⃣ UI Code

View (XML)

<mvc:View
  controllerName="demo.controller.Main"
  xmlns="sap.m"
  xmlns:mvc="sap.ui.core.mvc">

  <VBox>
    <Text id="userText" text="Loading user..." />
    
    <Table items="{/Persons}">
      <columns>
        <Column><Text text="Name"/></Column>
        <Column><Text text="Age"/></Column>
        <Column><Text text="Gender"/></Column>
      </columns>
      <items>
        <ColumnListItem>
          <cells>
            <Text text="{name}" />
            <Text text="{age}" />
            <Text text="{gender}" />
          </cells>
        </ColumnListItem>
      </items>
    </Table>

  </VBox>
</mvc:View>


---

Controller

onInit: function () {

  // Fetch logged-in user
  fetch("/personservice/getLoggedInUser()")
    .then(res => res.json())
    .then(data => {
      this.byId("userText")
          .setText("Logged in as: " + data.name);
    });

}


---

Runtime Behaviour

User A (User1Role):

Sees only persons age > 40

Sees their own login name


User B (User2Role):

Sees only persons age < 40

Sees their own login name


Filtering enforced in CAP backend. UI only displays returned data. Security intact.

End-to-end role-based dynamic data segregation with logged-in user display.